dialogue cohesion_engineer_knight
title: The teacher's rivets
trigger: Cohesion engineer knight level=2
once
speaker commander $commander
speaker engineer engineer
speaker knight knight

node open commander
  The Engineer is crouched beside the Knight's shield with a lamp, a thumbnail pressed to the back of the strap where it meets the iron. The Knight stands over both of them with arms folded.
  -> shear

node shear engineer
  This rivet's walking. See the shine round the head? It's been rocking every time you take a hit. Two more good ones and the strap comes off in your hand.
  -> teacher

node teacher knight
  My teacher set those rivets the winter I took the oath. Nobody's touched them since. They've held through worse than two good hits.
  -> worse

node worse engineer
  They held through worse when they were new. Metal gets tired. It doesn't care who set it. Commander, I can have a new one in before the fire's down. Tell the Knight.
  * Fix it tonight, Engineer. The rim and the old line stay untouched. -> fix
    do: AddCohesion engineer knight 10
    do: AddTrust knight -3
    do: SetFlag engineer_knight:rivet_fixed
  * The Knight does the work. Engineer, hand over the tools and talk it through. -> talk
    do: AddCohesion engineer knight 6
    do: SetFlag engineer_knight:rivet_taught
  * It's held this long. Leave the shield alone. -> leave
    do: AddCohesion engineer knight -4
    do: AddTrust engineer -2
    do: SetFlag engineer_knight:rivet_left
  * I stopped the wagon for the Engineer because a cracked axle needed someone to notice. Let the Engineer notice this. -> notice
    if: FlagSet engineer:list_axle
    do: AddCohesion engineer knight 8
    do: AddTrust engineer 2
    do: SetFlag engineer_knight:rivet_noticed

node fix knight
  Untouched. You hear that, Engineer? Not a scratch on the rim. Go on, then. I'll hold the lamp, so I can watch your hands.
  -> debt

node talk engineer
  Punch here. No, square to it. Tap, don't swing, it's not a ganger's head. There. You've got good hands for this, Knight. Wasted on hitting things.
  -> debt

node leave knight
  It'll hold. And if it doesn't, I'll learn something about my teacher I'd rather not know. Thank you for looking, though.
  -> debt

node notice knight
  Noticing's a kind of standing watch, I suppose. All right. Show me the shine first. I want to see what you saw.
  -> debt

node debt knight
  In the holds, a debt follows the family. My father's father owed a hall for a cow that died in the snow, and we paid it till I was ten. Is yours like that? This Redline debt?
  * Redline gets nothing. If they come to collect, they meet the shield first. -> shield
    if: FlagSet engineer:debt_defied
    do: AddCohesion engineer knight 10
    do: AddTrust knight 2
    do: SetFlag engineer_knight:debt_shield
  * The Knight's oath was to the hold's people. The Engineer is one of them now. -> people
    if: FlagSet knight:oath_people
    do: AddCohesion engineer knight 8
    do: SetFlag engineer_knight:debt_people
  * Work it out together, numbers and shield. Redline respects both. -> both
    do: AddCohesion engineer knight 8
    do: AddTrust engineer -2
    do: SetFlag engineer_knight:debt_both
  * That debt is the Engineer's to settle. The Knight has enough to stand before. -> own
    do: AddCohesion engineer knight 2
    do: SetFlag engineer_knight:debt_own

node shield engineer
  The shield first. With a new rivet in it, which I'd point out to them. Ha. I'd like to see a ganger read hold script.
  -> close

node people engineer
  One of the hold's. I've never been anybody's people. Redline had me on a list, and the list was all numbers. I think I'd rather be on yours, Knight.
  -> close

node both knight
  Numbers and a shield. I'll do the standing, you do the sums. If they argue with the sums, I stand closer.
  -> close

node own knight
  Your own to settle. All right. But if you go to settle it, Engineer, tell me first. I'd like to stand somewhere nearby, not doing anything.
  -> close

node close commander
  The old rivet goes into the Engineer's notebook, pressed flat between two pages. The Knight straps the shield on, works the arm twice, and doesn't say anything about how much better it sits.
